[I] Tool for interacting with Android A/B slots

[T] qbootctl is the Qualcomm bootctl HAL from AOSP, ported to build and run
[T] on musl and glibc Linux systems. It is used to query and switch the
[T] active A/B boot slot and mark boots successful on Qualcomm based phones
[T] and tablets.

[U] https://github.com/linux-msm/qbootctl

[A] Qbootctl Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

